\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Latent and observed causal structure of the generative model. Following standard PGM convention, circles/ellipses denote random variables and rectangles denote deterministic functions of their parents; shaded (colored) nodes are exported to the dataset, and white nodes with dashed outlines are latent and never exported. The outer plate is the per-student repetition ($i=1,\ldots  ,N$); the inner plate is the per-term repetition ($t=1,\ldots  ,T_i$, $T_i \le 8$), shown unrolled once across an adjacent term pair $t-1 \to t$ to make the prior-term-only dependency (red edges) visible, though the whole shaded band recurs every term: term $t$'s own Term Grade, Attendance Rate, and Financial Hold nodes are exactly the ``term $t-1$'' inputs to Eq.~\ref {eq:risk} in the next repetition of this plate, closing the loop that this single unrolled pair only shows one link of. Node fill colors match the phase color-coding used in Fig.~\ref {fig:pipeline}: purple for Phase 2 latent state, blue for Phase 3 observables, orange for the Phase 4 risk score and intervention, and red/pink for the Phase 5 hazard and dropout outcome. The Dropout Hazard node makes Eq.~\ref {eq:hazard} visually explicit.}}{9}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dag}{{2}{9}{Latent and observed causal structure of the generative model. Following standard PGM convention, circles/ellipses denote random variables and rectangles denote deterministic functions of their parents; shaded (colored) nodes are exported to the dataset, and white nodes with dashed outlines are latent and never exported. The outer plate is the per-student repetition ($i=1,\ldots ,N$); the inner plate is the per-term repetition ($t=1,\ldots ,T_i$, $T_i \le 8$), shown unrolled once across an adjacent term pair $t-1 \to t$ to make the prior-term-only dependency (red edges) visible, though the whole shaded band recurs every term: term $t$'s own Term Grade, Attendance Rate, and Financial Hold nodes are exactly the ``term $t-1$'' inputs to Eq.~\ref {eq:risk} in the next repetition of this plate, closing the loop that this single unrolled pair only shows one link of. Node fill colors match the phase color-coding used in Fig.~\ref {fig:pipeline}: purple for Phase 2 latent state, blue for Phase 3 observables, orange for the Phase 4 risk score and intervention, and red/pink for the Phase 5 hazard and dropout outcome. The Dropout Hazard node makes Eq.~\ref {eq:hazard} visually explicit}{figure.2}{}}
